  "about": "0069 fixed case list, DRAFT for root review; nothing has run. Routes are binding_oracle recordings, unchanged from 0065 and Astra's accepted shipping proofs. layout-* runs render nothing: the adapter creates no GPU device, and only the public layout/text snapshot and the numerical route record are kept. review-* renders 4 frames to settle spacing and copy; final-* then renders all 18 of its frames from the final source. Nothing is reused, so 22 frames are rendered in every case, under the 24-frame ceiling. Every GPU frame counts whether kept, compared or discarded; the runner debits a run's planned frames before it starts and never refunds a failed run. Each frame is one accept on a fresh single-use consumer of that host step's public render and UI input. Fresh rendering suits this sample, which has no temporal rendering state; no frame claims equivalence to an accumulated history. Frames at most 960x540, one process group at a time, 120 s per adapter child. Every adapter child, layout-only or not, first takes the global native GPU lock, then the packet lock, refusing at once if either is busy. These frames are the 'appearance' category; UI GPU regression tests (seven existing plus one newly added halo case) are planned separately in regression.json against their own 128-frame ceiling.",
